{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/49995-awesome-lunar-warforms-hybrid-body-rearrangements","id":49995,"title":"Awesome Lunar Warforms/Hybrid Body Rearrangements","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-15T12:46:02-08:00","id":49995,"title":"Awesome Lunar Warforms/Hybrid Body Rearrangements","content":"Since I brought it up in the topic on Lunar Spirit Shapes, I thought it'd be fun to have a place for people to talk about their favorite warforms and/or uses of Hybrid Body Rearrangement. Cool, creepy, creative - I want to hear about it, because shapeshifting is an awesome power and it can be used in a lot of really fun ways.<br /> <br /> My personal favorite is the warform of a Lunar I designed a while back. When DBT was activated, he went from angry wolf-man to giant angry wolf-man made of molten moonsilver with blazing red eyes. This led to being utterly terrifying in a fight, since you couldn't escape him, couldn't defend yourself against him (ever try parrying liquid metal?), and his movements borrowed from Arakune and Pyron.<br /> <br /> Your turn, forums!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T13:14:08-08:00","id":50018,"title":"","content":"I had a solar that once fought a Lunar of water. A ST creation sure... but Lunars can turn into rivers can't they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T13:18:52-08:00","id":50025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/49995-awesome-lunar-warforms-hybrid-body-rearrangements?p=50018#post50018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a solar that once fought a Lunar of water. A ST creation sure... but Lunars can turn into rivers can't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Just gotta eat a Water Elemental or a River God first.<br /> <br /> Or go questing out in the Wyld for appropriate mutations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T13:29:37-08:00","id":50030,"title":"","content":"There was one Lunar NPC I made once (with proper chargen rules no less, I was hoping to get to play him in an other game) who was an Angler-Fish totem trapper (don't remember his caste).<br /> <br /> His DBT (+HBR) had him become a 9-foot-tall monster with translucent black skin, needle-like teeth and a huge gaping Hideous Maw on his stomach.<br /> When he opened it, squid tentacles would shoot out to grapple his enemies and drag them into the Maw (for crushing and biting), enhanced by Claws of the Silver Moon and Impressions of Strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 01-15-2014, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T13:31:37-08:00","id":50032,"title":"","content":"Well, Ishi Singing-Tide is, of course, a whale. Specifically, he's one of those unreasonably huge can-pretend-to-be-an-island-covered-in-barnacles mythic whales. His War Form is... inspired by a certain bit of concept art for Cloverfield.<br /> <br /> Obviously, and sadly, he's not a valid starting character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T14:11:32-08:00","id":50062,"title":"","content":"My second attempt at an Exalted character was going to be this artistic Orgiastic Fugitive river pirate whose totem was the redtail catfish. His warform was going to be a handsomely whiskered dragon, a magnificent thing spewing clouds of opium smoke and boiling wine.<br /> Then I met the rules for Deadly Beastman Transformation, and he <i>ended</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T14:46:04-08:00","id":50097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/49995-awesome-lunar-warforms-hybrid-body-rearrangements?p=50032#post50032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Ishi Singing-Tide is, of course, a whale. Specifically, he's one of those unreasonably huge can-pretend-to-be-an-island-covered-in-barnacles mythic whales. His War Form is... inspired by a certain bit of concept art for Cloverfield.<br /> <br /> Obviously, and sadly, he's not a valid starting character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rulelawyering impulse overtaking...<br /> I think he is valid. You need:<br /> TOWERING BEAST FORM to have whale spirit shape,<br /> Essence 3 &amp; HYBRID BODY REARRANGEMENT (errated version) for extra limbs, and for taking gargantuan mutation three times (depending on your ST it either makes your whale <b>ten times </b>bigger or <b>sixty four</b> times bigger).<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://wpc.556e.edgecastcdn.net/80556E/img.news/NE7T7ba8AdEHa8_1_1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Something like this should be possible with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1673-runelord","name":"Runelord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T14:55:38-08:00","id":50111,"title":"","content":"The one Lunar I played had a sun bear totem, and looked in my mind to be effectively a human sized mass of fuzz and claws. Things got silly, though, when I got a Girdle of the Chtonic Baara, and became a Bearodactyl. This, in turn, led to Bearodactyl Riders, as everyone in the circle wanted to ride me, so as to avoid reprisal from other combatants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T15:28:30-08:00","id":50157,"title":"","content":"I'd really love to play a spider-totem Lunar one day, with a drider-like warform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T15:57:16-08:00","id":50187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/49995-awesome-lunar-warforms-hybrid-body-rearrangements?p=50097#post50097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rulelawyering impulse overtaking...<br /> I think he is valid. You need:<br /> TOWERING BEAST FORM to have whale spirit shape,<br /> Essence 3 &amp; HYBRID BODY REARRANGEMENT (errated version) for extra limbs, and for taking gargantuan mutation three times (depending on your ST it either makes your whale <b>ten times </b>bigger or <b>sixty four</b> times bigger).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://wpc.556e.edgecastcdn.net/80556E/img.news/NE7T7ba8AdEHa8_1_1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://wpc.556e.edgecastcdn.net/80556E/img.news/NE7T7ba8AdEHa8_1_1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://wpc.556e.edgecastcdn.net/80556E/img.news/NE7T7ba8AdEHa8_1_1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://wpc.556e.edgecastcdn.net/80556E/img.news/NE7T7ba8AdEHa8_1_1.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> Something like this should be possible with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>HBR can't alter your entire form, so you can't use it to just get bigger. That's why Mountainous Spirit Exercise, Emperor-Ox Expansion and God-Beast Transcendence are all distinct Knacks.<br /> <br /> That said, a starting Mokole in Werewolf, assuming Gnosis 10, can get close to that bulk, if not achieve it (five purchases of Tall, three of Behemoth, you'll have to talk to your ST about adjusting the mass increase per purchase so it triples instead of doubles with each purchase). So, that could form the core of an argument to ease up on the prerequisites to the size-increasing shapeshifting powers available to the Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T16:00:53-08:00","id":50193,"title":"","content":"I've never had a chance to be a really cool Warform Lunar, but I've been in games with two of them. One was a stag totem No Moon, whose DBT was basically a Keeper of the Grove from WarCraft. The other somehow got from having a squirrel totem to a Warform that could easily be mistaken for a cross between a chameleon and a zergling with added tentacles. His/her favorite trick was to stealth around a battle and grab people with a ridiculously long tongue, then disembowel them before selecting another target.<br /> <br /> Naturally, the second one's nickname was &quot;Fluffy.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T16:00:59-08:00","id":50194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/49995-awesome-lunar-warforms-hybrid-body-rearrangements?p=50097#post50097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rulelawyering impulse overtaking...<br /> I think he is valid. You need:<br /> TOWERING BEAST FORM to have whale spirit shape,<br /> Essence 3 &amp; HYBRID BODY REARRANGEMENT (errated version) for extra limbs, and for taking gargantuan mutation three times (depending on your ST it either makes your whale <b>ten times </b>bigger or <b>sixty four</b> times bigger).<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://wpc.556e.edgecastcdn.net/80556E/img.news/NE7T7ba8AdEHa8_1_1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Something like this should be possible with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd been under the impression that pumping the war form up to that kind of scale explicitly required Emperor Ox Expansion, but if a GM'd let me get away with it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T16:06:33-08:00","id":50198,"title":"","content":"I was going to make my horse-aspected No Moon archer into a centaur, but the game ended about the time I was going to get the warform upgrade knack. Extra limbs are really expensive to get, hehe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T16:29:35-08:00","id":50218,"title":"","content":"I sort of want to build a spider-totem lunar with emperor ox, pick up a bunch of insect- and arthropod-based heart's bloods, and basically make a horrifying insectoid kaiju war-form with a scorpion's tail, beetle wings, a crab's claws, and more besides","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T17:51:27-08:00","id":50286,"title":"","content":"This might be my ego talking but I don't think there's a cooler animal than a human anywhere in existence. So my ideal Lunar builds her entire arsenal of techniques around uses of Hybrid Body Rearrangement, taking only the parts that she needs at any given moment. Her warform would never be the same thing twice, because it would be a list of whatever mutations she needed to gain every possible advantage in that specific encounter. No mere animal would ever meet her needs except as spare parts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T18:12:43-08:00","id":50305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/49995-awesome-lunar-warforms-hybrid-body-rearrangements?p=50194#post50194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd been under the impression that pumping the war form up to that kind of scale explicitly required Emperor Ox Expansion, but if a GM'd let me get away with it...</div> </div> </div> </div>This does not assume war form, just spirit form and HBR.<br /> <br /> It seams that &quot;size mutations&quot; break the system in this case. It allows you to sidestep DBT + DOE. Three gargantuan mutation give you +12 on strength and stamina, plus shitload of health levels. Kinda stronger than war form. This might not be what the Devs intended.<br /> <br /> *Saur Ops Specialist that's an interesting reading... &quot;You can learn to change just part of your body.&quot;<br /> <b>We demand Developer input.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1673-runelord","user":"Runelord","date":". 01-15-2014, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1673-runelord","name":"Runelord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T19:29:51-08:00","id":51302,"title":"","content":"Would a Centaur be a good warform? or is that just a Wyld Mutant tribe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T16:17:36-08:00","id":51954,"title":"","content":"1. Best options for Hybrid Body Rearrangement, in my opinion: Wings, Serpent's Body, Talons, Armored Hide.<br /> <br /> 2. <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eKPrGxB1Kzc&amp;t=36s\" target=\"_blank\">Pistol shrimp</a> totem, with Greater Natural Missile and Talons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/49995-awesome-lunar-warforms-hybrid-body-rearrangements?p=50062#post50062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My second attempt at an Exalted character was going to be this artistic Orgiastic Fugitive river pirate whose totem was the redtail catfish.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have excellent taste in siluriformes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":832,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/832-surlyseraph","user":"SurlySeraph","date":". 01-17-2014, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/832-surlyseraph","name":"SurlySeraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T17:01:12-08:00","id":51983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/49995-awesome-lunar-warforms-hybrid-body-rearrangements?p=51302#post51302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a Centaur be a good warform? or is that just a Wyld Mutant tribe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not both?<br /> Of course, the 2e DBT would be pretty terrible at making you a cool centaur, at least to begin with (the extra legs alone cost 6 mutation points), but idea is good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T18:19:56-08:00","id":56496,"title":"","content":"I have one White Owl totem (second only to Wolves and Foxes, I know) character whose DBT is for all intents and purposes an angel, and plays the part too. It suits the character because of his Motivation; he's big on the &quot;Steward of Creation&quot; part, protecting the innocent and so on. At the same time, he subverts it somewhat by being very much Old Testament about the things he doesn't like, like slavers; turning into a swarm of insects, smiting people with pillars of flame, eating the souls of the wicked that he may cleanse them of evil... Also, he's a romantic fool who is certain his &quot;Better Half&quot; will be a kind, beautiful woman, and together they'll bring peace and prosperity to the world while living happily ever after. In truth? Four words; <i>He</i> is a <u>Fiend</u>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T00:06:37-08:00","id":56606,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for a Full Moon with the totem/spirit shape of a Tyrant Lizard. Prolly an old NPC, who in is heyday was the leader of the Tyrant Guard: guys who took spirit shape of Tyrant Lizards obviously :P<br /> <br /> Their DBT would be something like the Krogan from Mass Effect: Lizard like with great strength and soak/stamina/healing-factor like stuff. Ultimate Shock Troopers and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T10:17:41-08:00","id":57494,"title":"","content":"I'm strongly of the opinion that Hybrid Body Rearrangement, by itself, should not allow size mutations. You'd need the appropriate knacks such as Humble Mouse Shape to expand your size limits.<br /> <br /> <br /> Some of my Hybrid Body Rearrangement tricks:<br /> <br /> -First off, Lunar Blood Shaping Technique. Ask your ST if you can use LBST+HBR to mutate your friends. (Potentially get an upgrade to combine them.) If you can, awesome.<br /> <br /> -Anything with Multiple Limbs (usually Arms). Asura's Wrath combat style FTW. Reduces multiple action penalties and lets you wield a two-handed weapon together with a shield, while leaving a hand free to make obscene gestures.<br /> <br /> -Emerald Grasshopper Form to turn into something small, then manifest Scorpion's Tail (twice to give it Piercing if you want), and Toxin however many times you feel like stacking that. Instant assassin skills, no training required! (It's never spelled out anywhere specific that EGF tiny forms are particularly stealthy, but the guideline I'd use is that enemies have -3 or -4 external penalty to attack or spot you, based on the Minuscule mutation in Compass:Wyld.) You can top it off with Chameleon if you want even more stealth.<br /> <br /> -Inexhaustible. Not the most powerful, but definitely one of the most convenient mutations out there. Never suffer fatigue. Run all day. Stand watch all night, or at least those nights where you can spare the willpower since you won't get to roll Conviction. (For extra fun: Lunar Blood Shaping Technique to give your lover Inexhaustible as well. Impossible Joints makes this even more fun.)<br /> <br /> -Mobility mutations: Gills and Wings are in the corebook, yet still largely overlooked in most of the games I've played. Being able to traverse sea and air opens up a lot of new travel options. On land, Cheetah's Pace increases regular travel speed. If you want to remain stationary up where you are, or lack Wings for whatever reason, Spider Legs (in Manual:Lunars) lets you climb a vertical surface and hang from the ceiling, also +4 jumps. Brachiation belongs on this list too; it's perhaps not all that good compared to the others, but funny.<br /> <br /> -If you dare touch the PITA that is clinch rules, combine Serpent's Body (+4 on clinch rolls), Prehensile Body Hair (+3 str for clinch) and Acidic Pustules (all in Lunars) with Quills from the corebook. Note that Quills is stackable. You may want to get a few purchases of Tentacles and Extra Arms too if the ST will let you clinch more than one person that way. Hilarity ensues if this is done while a small form, as the +7 bonus to clinches probably outweighs whatever Strength loss you get from the small size. (Idea: describe this as being a thorn vine wrapping around the opponent.)<br /> <br /> -Dragon's Breath. Not very effective, but awesome. Notable in that it can be aimed with Athletics.<br /> <br /> -Night Vision, Keen Senses, etc. and the big one, Lidless Demon Eye. Very hard to get (you'd need Green Sun Child at a minimum and some demon-sorting... or maybe Taste of Luna's Champions and ask an elder) but very powerful. Automatically detect invisible creatures, see dematerialized creatures, sense Essence as though you had used All-Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight.<br /> <br /> -Speaking of Taste of Luna's Champions, consider asking your ST to waive the per-shape experience cost in favor of paying xp for increased Heart's Blood background, and perhaps paying temporary Willpower for the individual shapes you're copying. As written, I find this Knack very unappealing due to the disproportionate XP cost compared to hunting the form, especially considering as you'd need the appropriate hunting knack for esoteric shapes anyway.<br /> <br /> -Armored Hide, +4L natural soak, always nice if you get into a fight, only costs 3m and isn't committed. Also +4 dice on Survival rolls, which should probably be interpreted narrowly. Upgrade is Stone Body for +6L, but that penalizes Dexterity which is usually a bad idea.<br /> <br /> -(Element) Adaptation. Definitely requires Luna's Hidden Face (LHF makes several of the above easier but probably isn't required for them), and functions sort of like the discount version of Directional Mastery Technique.<br /> <br /> -Semi-Bullshit: Depending on your ST, learn Green Sun Child so you can hunt demons, then pick some of the demonic mutations from Manual:Infernals. (I wouldn't allow this because I think they should be Flaws, but it's worth mentioning.) Ordination of Lies boosts your social rolls, Blurred Fate helps hide from divination, Gatekeeper shows you portals to Cecelyne, etc.<br /> <br /> -Total Bullshit: Scroll of Heroes mutations pretty much universally fall into this category. Ban them. Ban them with the great banhammer. In particular, ban Essence Abundance and its +16 motepool. Should definitely not be possible to manifest this for 4m with Hybrid Body Rearrangement, even if the Lunar does hunt and eat a God-Blood. Should probably not be a mutation at all, but a god-blood-only merit. Only use these if you're playing in the sort of game where the Brutal Attack merit is allowed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":960,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/960-erikm","user":"ErikM","date":". 01-25-2014, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/960-erikm","name":"ErikM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T11:36:46-08:00","id":57543,"title":"","content":"I generally approach Stone Body as simply just going for soak and not including the alteration to Attributes, since it's screwy and incongruous, and altering Attributes outside of size-altering mutations is generally not so great an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T13:54:25-08:00","id":57617,"title":"","content":"Following the serious advice, here's a more silly combination of mutations: Extra Arms, Spider Legs (4 in one go), Quills (stackable), Tentacles (stackable), Tail (or Serpent's Body if you want to turn up the monster factor), Horns, Fangs, Claws, Wings, Terrifying Mane, Prehensile Body Hair, Chameleon's Tongue.<br /> <br /> Oh god it has bits sticking out everywhere!<br /> <br /> You should probably not have the Chameleon's Tongue emerge from a Hideous Maw elsewhere on your snake body unless you're deliberately trying to terrorize people and bait the Wyld Hunt into coming. ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/960-erikm","name":"ErikM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T09:12:00-08:00","id":58122,"title":"","content":"Sticks to the Hulls of Ships, was a Sea Cucumber totem Lunar, looked kind of like a Heedra from the Nausicaa manga. Big rubbery body, every single healing advantage/charm up at all times. Had a custom charm where whenever he took damage the piece fell off, animated and became an extra for the scene. Also had an attack where he would vomit out his sticky intestines at people (the actual animal does it out the other end, but that is a little too gross) Was a reoccurring NPC villain, teamed up and was posesed by Hun-tha for more hilarity.<br /> Here is a Heedra, he looked kind of like this but with a feathery tentacle filled mouth.<br /> <img src=\"http://4.bp.blogspot.com/_oKPGQNEEU5o/SNnBj3_573I/AAAAAAAAADE/pEj5CM983Kw/s400/Yupa_Heedra_web.jpg<i>\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></i><br /> <br /> Had another archer whos totem was a Lionfish, Fishperson covered in venomous spines plus water adaptation. She was a sniper and used her quills as arrowheads to shoot at boats passing overhead using the eyes of Seagulls to hit her targets.<br /> Looked kind of like this but with legs and a moonsilver powebow.<br /> <img src=\"http://th01.deviantart.net/fs5/PRE/i/2004/337/c/1/Lionfish_Mermaid_by_zepheenia.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/363-muscadomestica","name":"MuscaDomestica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T13:25:44-08:00","id":60084,"title":"","content":"This one's not so much the form itself, but tricks done with it.<br /> <br /> My Lunar is Essence 7 and yet still does not have a warform. He has no need for one.<br /> <br /> Instead, he hunts river dragons, taking their shapes and twisting them - giving them arms and speech, and basically molding them into warstriders, which shape he then lends to troops under his command via Lunar Blood Shaping Technique. These are awakened mortals with artifacts to hold warstrider weapons Elsewhere. Tens to hundreds of warstriders out of nowhere, without needing to maintain them, is useful for many things - such as ambushing Wyld Hunt legions by letting them try to invade his city. (They didn't even get to the walls.)<br /> <br /> When he travels, he has a stryx form: strong enough to carry significant payloads, airborne so he doesn't care if there's a mountain range or a sea in the way, and fast enough (with Charm help, motes committed for the duration) to cross a Direction in under a week.<br /> <br /> True, he lacks conventional combat prowess. His personal combats tend to turn out like his most recent combat: he stole incriminating evidence from some raksha and lead them on a short chase - kiting them into a waiting Dusk with 8 30+ die attacks per tick, a Solar with Sorcery ready, and a Lunar with...well, let's just say the combat was short, and that was before his Mate showed up. That, in turn, was before he left for about 2 actions, bringing an entire fae court down on what remained. (Or at least their queen, but she came alone since there wasn't need for more power by that point, and was ready to summon her guards if needed.) His spirit shape is a housecat for many reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/240-winged-cat","name":"Winged Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar240_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T10:01:14-08:00","id":60867,"title":"","content":"I never got to play him but Swims in Strange Waters was going to be a lunar with a giant squid heart beast and a warform with a bunch tentacles instead of legs. He was going to be a heavily tanned islander who exalted somewhere remote in the West then spent a long time swimming around on the border of the wyld before being found by the silver pact. He was also going to have a few points of permanent limit and permanent mutations, leathery skin and gills I think it was. And mainly have change part of your body / mutation related charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1732-snowy","name":"Snowy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T02:12:21-08:00","id":67800,"title":"","content":"A couple years ago I was running my annual Halloween game, so I tried squicking the players out a bit. This game was a side story. They were playing Dragon Blooded members of a Wyld Hunt who had been long reoccuring foes/occasional friends with the player's characters in the main campaign.<br /> <br /> I created a Lunar antagonist based around the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhizocephala\" target=\"_blank\">Rhizocephala.</a> A better description of one can be found <a href=\"http://deepseanews.com/2013/10/this-may-be-the-oceans-most-horrifying-monster-and-youve-probably-never-heard-of-it/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. <br /> <br /> She functioned like a parasite taking over people's bodies and turning them into walking incubators for her creepy monster-babies. <br /> <br /> I constructed a new Knack, which allowed her to merge her body into another and take control of the victim as a Disease effect. She had further improved the technique allowing her to merge with and control up to a dozen victims who would explode into monster babies when killed. Her goal was to eventually be able to infest everyone in Creation, though fortunately the players managed to stop her well before she had the chance. <br /> <br /> It was just a oneshot, but she became a memorable character and even now every time Lunars get mentioned someone will say, &quot;The Immaculate Order is right! KILL THEM ALL WITH FIRE!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T13:45:53-08:00","id":68055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/49995-awesome-lunar-warforms-hybrid-body-rearrangements?p=67800#post67800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple years ago I was running my annual Halloween game, so I tried squicking the players out a bit. This game was a side story. They were playing Dragon Blooded members of a Wyld Hunt who had been long reoccuring foes/occasional friends with the player's characters in the main campaign.<br /> <br /> I created a Lunar antagonist based around the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhizocephala\" target=\"_blank\">Rhizocephala.</a> A better description of one can be found <a href=\"http://deepseanews.com/2013/10/this-may-be-the-oceans-most-horrifying-monster-and-youve-probably-never-heard-of-it/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> She functioned like a parasite taking over people's bodies and turning them into walking incubators for her creepy monster-babies.<br /> <br /> I constructed a new Knack, which allowed her to merge her body into another and take control of the victim as a Disease effect. She had further improved the technique allowing her to merge with and control up to a dozen victims who would explode into monster babies when killed. Her goal was to eventually be able to infest everyone in Creation, though fortunately the players managed to stop her well before she had the chance.<br /> <br /> It was just a oneshot, but she became a memorable character and even now every time Lunars get mentioned someone will say, &quot;The Immaculate Order is right! KILL THEM ALL WITH FIRE!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Chryssalids. Chryssalids everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T13:41:13-08:00","id":68621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/49995-awesome-lunar-warforms-hybrid-body-rearrangements?p=50062#post50062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My second attempt at an Exalted character was going to be this artistic Orgiastic Fugitive river pirate whose totem was the redtail catfish. His warform was going to be a handsomely whiskered dragon, a magnificent thing spewing clouds of opium smoke and boiling wine.<br /> Then I met the rules for Deadly Beastman Transformation, and he <i>ended</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Few good character concepts survive Exalted's shitty rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/218-two-shadows","name":"Two-Shadows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar218_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T14:00:13-08:00","id":68630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Two-Shadows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/49995-awesome-lunar-warforms-hybrid-body-rearrangements?p=68621#post68621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Few good character concepts survive Exalted's shitty rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Barring a single Dragon-Blooded sorcerer, pretty much all of my non-Lunar concepts have made it through chargen, though not necessarily further. Meanwhile, every single Lunar idea has died at the hands of the monster known as Prerequisite Excellency.<br /> <br /> Well, technically, the experimental Lunars M\u00f8rke wanted made it through, but they were mere shadows of what I actually tried to make them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:09:43-07:00","id":223529,"title":"","content":"Has anyone made something like an Akylosaurus? I was thinking about Limb Shielding Growth and it just seems to be interesting. Oh and yes dinosaurs better exist damn it, I don't care if there aren't any good examples they need to exist in the south west competing with lions and simhatas...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:30:46-07:00","id":223563,"title":"","content":"My new Lunar Oza uses a combination of her human and Tree Pard shapes with a few others thrown in. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/vDBMDHo.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:41:25-07:00","id":223571,"title":"","content":"I once played a Lunar in Gunstar Autochthonia. We didn't get far enough for my Lunar to do what he wanted to do, which was hunt down and kill demon-fighters, then starships, and eventually megaships all made out of demons. After that, go hunt down and eat the giant star-scorpion thing, and hybrid that thing into my DBT. The other thing I had was becoming a lemur and acting as the exotic pet of one of the other characters, who would hand me to a poor unsuspecting individual, where I would sit on his shoulder and use my trademark 'One Inch Lemur Punch' to punch him in the side of the head. That part I got to do lots because Lemurs with MA 5 punch stupidly well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:54:01-07:00","id":223583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citadel97501</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/49995-awesome-lunar-warforms-hybrid-body-rearrangements?p=223529#post223529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone made something like an Akylosaurus? I was thinking about Limb Shielding Growth and it just seems to be interesting. Oh and yes dinosaurs better exist damn it, I don't care if there aren't any good examples they need to exist in the south west competing with lions and simhatas...</div> </div> </div> </div>The dinosaur aesthetic is pretty solidly taken by Dragon Kings, barring claw striders and tyrant lizards. Which is kind of a shame, really, it'd make sense for other kinds of dinosaur-esque mundane creatures to exist considering all the post-dinosaur megafauna that are present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:54:37-07:00","id":223584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citadel97501</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/49995-awesome-lunar-warforms-hybrid-body-rearrangements?p=223529#post223529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone made something like an Akylosaurus? I was thinking about Limb Shielding Growth and it just seems to be interesting. Oh and yes dinosaurs better exist damn it, I don't care if there aren't any good examples they need to exist in the south west competing with lions and simhatas...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I went with <i>Euoplacephalus</i> for one character. Smaller, but even more armored, right down to the eyelids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T13:57:27-07:00","id":223589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citadel97501</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/49995-awesome-lunar-warforms-hybrid-body-rearrangements?p=223529#post223529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone made something like an Akylosaurus? I was thinking about Limb Shielding Growth and it just seems to be interesting. Oh and yes dinosaurs better exist damn it, I don't care if there aren't any good examples they need to exist in the south west competing with lions and simhatas...</div> </div> </div> </div>Claw Striders and Tyrant Lizards exist. There's your Theropods. The others exist as Dragon-Kings, and probably exist as regular animals as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T14:48:37-07:00","id":223617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/49995-awesome-lunar-warforms-hybrid-body-rearrangements?p=223589#post223589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Claw Striders and Tyrant Lizards exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also river dragons. And raitons and mospids, as scaled birds, aren't technically dinosaurs but still pretty damn close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 08-09-2014, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T15:40:43-07:00","id":223666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/49995-awesome-lunar-warforms-hybrid-body-rearrangements?p=223617#post223617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also river dragons. And raitons and mospids, as scaled birds, aren't technically dinosaurs but still pretty damn close.</div> </div> </div> </div>River dragons aren't dinosaurs. Birds are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T16:16:42-07:00","id":223691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/49995-awesome-lunar-warforms-hybrid-body-rearrangements?p=223666#post223666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">River dragons aren't dinosaurs. Birds are.</div> </div> </div> </div>River dragons are described as having a rudder-like tail, huge flippers and a long serpentine neck. They are pretty clearly <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/search?hl=fr&amp;site=imghp&amp;tbm=isch&amp;source=hp&amp;biw=1231&amp;bih=672&amp;q=plesiosaurids&amp;oq=plesiosaurids&amp;gs_l=img.3...24459.24459.0.25029.1.1.0.0.0.0.206.206.2-1.1.0....0...1ac..51.img..1.0.0.YTuIO1Gdrt0#hl=fr&amp;q=Plesiosauroidea&amp;spell=1&amp;tbm=isch\" target=\"_blank\">plesiosauroids</a>.<br /> <br /> The picture is all wrong, of course. But then, mospids and raitons don't have scales in their pictures, and the claw strider looks like a tiny T-rex instead of Utahraptor. Hell, the mospid is described as being scaled with feather tufts on its thumbs and tail. It looks like a feathered bird with fins on its tail, because apparently reversing the description is what all the cool kids do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T16:24:05-07:00","id":223694,"title":"","content":"I think river dragons are mote intended to be pliosauroids than plesiosauroids. And that doesn't account for river dragons appearing more amphibious in nature than wholly marine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T16:33:18-07:00","id":223696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/49995-awesome-lunar-warforms-hybrid-body-rearrangements?p=223694#post223694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think river dragons are mote intended to be pliosauroids than plesiosauroids. And that doesn't account for river dragons appearing more amphibious in nature than wholly marine.</div> </div> </div> </div>What part of &quot;long serpentine neck&quot; says pliosauroidea to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T16:52:33-07:00","id":223714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-e